{
  "_doc": {
    "purpose": "Per-country local-road fleet and dwelling-trip priors; country-fleet.ts derives the service-tree model directly from this one cited table.",
    "quantities": {
      "moto_fleet_share": "powered 2-/3-wheelers as share of total REGISTERED vehicles (ownership). A PRIOR only — a motorcycle drives fewer daily km than a truck, so ownership share overstates traffic share.",
      "moto_traffic_share": "share of powered 2-/3-wheelers in daily vehicle FLOW on local roads (what splitAADT writes into aadt_moto). Derived by country-fleet.ts as factor(continent) x moto_fleet_share clamped to [0.01, 0.45] (Asia 0.40, Europe/NA/Oceania 0.15, SA 0.20 — usage intensity differs; Africa never derives, registration misses informal fleets), unless moto_traffic_share_override is set.",
      "moto_traffic_share_override": "traffic-calibrated value taken from a national enricher's split tables (population-weighted blend of its regional tiers) — always wins over the derived prior.",
      "vehicle_trips_per_occupied_dwelling": "motor-vehicle trips per OCCUPIED dwelling (household) per day, both directions, annual average, all vehicle classes incl. motorcycles — entered in the surveys' native unit. country-fleet.ts multiplies by 0.92 stock occupancy (OECD HM1-1) because the trip model counts GFA-estimated STOCK dwellings; the generated field is tripsPerDwelling (per stock dwelling). WORLD 3.68 already folds the factor in (4.0 base x 0.92) and is exempt."
    },
    "refresh": "Review updates to the cited source observations and calibrated overrides here; country-fleet.ts derives runtime values without a second generated table."
  },
